  "description": "Talk about your body, express aches, and describe how you feel.",
  "guidebook": "### Talking About Health in German\n\nWhen you don't feel well, German offers simple ways to express it!\n\nTo describe pain, use the separable verb **wehtun** (to hurt):\n- *Mein Kopf tut weh.* (My head hurts.)\n- *Meine Augen tun weh.* (My eyes hurt – notice plural *tun*!)\n\nTo describe how you are feeling, combine **sein** (to be) with adjectives:\n- *Ich bin müde.* (I am tired.)\n- *Er ist krank.* (He is sick.)\n\nWhen heading to get help, pay attention to contracted prepositions:\n- **zum Arzt** (to the doctor – *zu* + *dem*)\n- **ins Krankenhaus** (into the hospital – *in* + *das*)\n\nGute Besserung (Get well soon)!",
